# Backstage specifications

Technical Specifications (`/technical-specifications`) is the pull and push page. A successful push writes `backstage_specifications` through `App\Services\ProductMaster\BackstageSpecificationStore`.

Each row is the latest non-blank value pushed for one SKU, marketplace, and specification name, plus the category used for that marketplace.

When a marketplace push needs item specifics or attributes:

- Read `latestForSku($sku, $marketplace)` and map matching names. Do not ask for those values.
- Call `missingForSku($sku, $requiredNames, $marketplace)` and prompt only for the names it returns.
- After a successful push, call `recordPush($sku, $marketplace, $specs)`. Blank values are not stored.
- Do not mention backstage data unless the task is a marketplace specification push.
